From: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5) <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: load firmware before probe IPC sync

The BPI-R4 Pro 8X AS21010PB1 PHYs can expose empty C45 IDs before the
firmware path has settled.  After the DT-declared PHY ID fallback lets the
AS21010PB1 entry bind directly, probe reaches aeon_ipc_sync_parity()
without first running the generic AS21xxx firmware pre-pass.

Runtime on r0+37889-d91102e6e4 shows exactly that failure:

  mdio_bus mdio-bus:1c: Invalid IPC status on sync parity: 0
  Aeonsemi AS21010PB1 mdio-bus:1c: aeon_ipc_wait_cmd failed: -110
  Aeonsemi AS21010PB1 mdio-bus:1c: probe ... failed with error -110

The vendor AS21xxx driver loads firmware at the start of probe before
synchronizing IPC.  Preserve the upstream-style generic firmware pre-pass,
but also load firmware in probe when the DT node explicitly provides a
firmware-name.  This keeps non-firmware-described AS21xxx users on the
existing path while restoring the vendor-required ordering for BPI-R4 Pro
8X.

Behavior source: Banana Pi BPI-R4 Pro 8X vendor as21xxx.c probe path and
local r0+37889-d91102e6e4 serial runtime evidence.

Adapted-by: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5)
---
 drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -643,6 +643,14 @@ static int as21xxx_probe(struct phy_devi
 	 */
 	phydev->c45_ids.devices_in_package &= ~BIT(0);
 
+	if (phydev->mdio.dev.of_node &&
+	    of_find_property(phydev->mdio.dev.of_node,
+			     "firmware-name", NULL)) {
+		ret = aeon_firmware_load(phydev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	ret = aeon_ipc_sync_parity(phydev, priv);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
